1. Executive Summary
This report documents a security assessment of the OWASP Juice Shop application running in a local Docker-based testing environment on Windows.

The assessment focused on two vulnerability classes: SQL Injection and Cross-Site Scripting (XSS). The objective was to understand the vulnerabilities, document reproducible evidence, evaluate potential security impact, and provide actionable remediation recommendations.

The findings documented in this report are limited to the local training environment. Results should not be interpreted as evidence of exposure in a production application.

Assessment status: Findings require supporting evidence and final validation before this report is considered complete.

2. Assessment Objectives

    Identify and document SQL Injection and XSS behaviour in the authorized training application.
    Record reproducible testing steps and supporting evidence.
    Assess potential confidentiality, integrity, and availability impacts.
    Map verified findings to applicable OWASP categories.
    Calculate CVSS 3.1 scores using evidence-based attack scenarios.
    Recommend developer fixes and operational controls.
    Establish remediation and retesting priorities.

3. Scope and Rules of Engagement

In scope

    The locally hosted OWASP Juice Shop application.
