6. Finding VAPT-001 — SQL Injection

Description
SQL Injection can occur when an application incorporates untrusted input into a database query without 
appropriate parameterization. Depending on the affected query and database permissions,
exploitation may allow unauthorized data access or authentication logic bypass.
Reproduction procedure

    Open the authorized local Juice Shop instance.
    Navigate to the affected functionality.
    Record the exact test conditions and input used.
    Document the actual application response.
    Repeat the test safely to confirm reproducibility.
    Preserve the evidence without exposing credentials or personal data

7. Finding VAPT-002 — Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)

Description

Cross-Site Scripting can occur when untrusted content is interpreted as executable script in a browser. The precise risk depends on the injection context, affected page, browser execution, and privileges of the affected user.

Affected component: [Insert verified endpoint, feature, or rendering context]

Evidence: [Insert XSS-Evidence-01.png and relevant sanitized details]

Reproduction procedure

    Open the authorized local Juice Shop instance.
    Navigate to the affected feature.
    Record the test input and the context in which it is processed.
    Document the actual browser behaviour.
    Confirm whether script execution occurred and whether it is reproducible.
    Preserve screenshots and sanitized supporting evidence.

